From aa1c1082bc0aba28c746d230a94dabc60d169b79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:02:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] realtime: publish ids and actions, never records

The realtime stream reaches every signed-in user in the tenant whatever they
may read, and publishers attached the whole record to the event: carriers
with their tax ids, customers, users, invoices, proposals, plans, runs,
watchtower items, shipment comments and holds, notifications addressed to a
role. Anyone with the stream open could read them.

PublishResourceInvalidationRequest, ResourceInvalidationEvent,
realtimeinvalidation.PublishParams, RecordChange, ChangeOf and
ShipmentInvalidation no longer have an entity field, so no publisher can
attach a record again. An event names the record (recordId) and, where a
screen needs to know what it belongs to, its parent (parentId: an artifact's
or schedule's conversation, a billing queue item's or rating review's
shipment, a document's owning record, a dispute's invoice, a capture
request's device). Every publisher is converted; the invoice realtime
snapshot, the turn announcement payload and realtime.maxEntityBytes are
gone. The EDI status publish no longer reads the invoice back just to build
a snapshot. The capture device stream builds its signal from the ids.
Notifications now carry their id, which they never did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
