-- **Large entities.** An event whose encoded entity is larger than
-  `maxEntityBytes` is sent without it; the reader refetches instead of patching.
+- **Identifiers, never records.** An event says which record changed and how:
+  `resource`, `action`, `recordId`, and `parentId` when a screen needs to know
+  what the record belongs to (the conversation an artifact or schedule is in, the
+  shipment a billing queue item or rating review is about, the record a document
+  is filed on, the invoice a dispute is about, the device a capture request is
+  for). It never carries the record, or any field of it, because the stream
+  reaches everyone signed in to the tenant whatever they may read. A screen that
+  needs the record refetches it through a read that checks permission
+  (`invalidateQueries`, or one read by id such as the watchtower item or the
+  notification feed). There is no entity field on the request, so this cannot
+  come back by accident; field names (`fields`), the record version and the actor
+  are the only other metadata.
 - **Portal readers** (drivers in Dash) receive an event not addressed to them
-  without `entity` and `fields`: they learn that a kind of record changed, never
-  what it now says.
+  without `fields`: they learn that a kind of record changed, nothing more.
 
