From 5ec3aa6a06d1d3cb81232cf4382f65f5a7aed827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:21:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] realtime: refetch through checked reads instead of
 reading the event

The web app and Dash read records straight off realtime events: rows were
patched from the event's entity, notification toasts came from the
notification on the event (including notifications addressed to a role, sent
to the whole tenant), comment threads were patched from the comment, the
watchtower queue from the item, invoice toasts from an invoice snapshot, and
the case rail and artifact routing from fields of the entity.

Events now carry ids only, so every consumer reads through the queries that
check permission:
- list rows refetch instead of being patched (the patch code is gone);
- a notification event names its id, and the toast reads it from the
  person's own feed (notificationService.findInFeed), so a notice for
  someone else or for a role they do not hold toasts nothing;
- a shipment comment event refetches that shipment's thread and count, and
  someone else's top-level comment moves the new-comments pill; replies are
  published as "replied" so they do not;
- the watchtower queue moves once the item is read again;
- the open invoice toasts by comparing the refetched invoice with what it
  last showed, and an automatic post failure by the event's action and actor;
- cases and artifact lists match on recordId and parentId;
- turn events are addressed to their owner, so the client filter on the
  entity's userId is gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
